<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    Launcher icon, built the way the stock Mudita Kompakt apps build theirs
    (read from the on-device Calculator / Camera / Notes icons): a plain 81dp
    vector rather than an adaptive icon, so the launcher draws it edge to edge
    with no raster resampling and no system icon mask.
    - Design: the artist's rendition received 2026-11-20, redrawn as a vector.
      The border is the stock Mudita ring; everything inside it is the artwork
      as drawn: its line weight, its corner radius, and its eight arm ends
      where the artist put them (they are not symmetric: the bottom gap is
      narrower than the other three; do not even them out).
      Measurements: icons/launcher.svg.
    - Border: Mudita's exact ring: 2.5 thick (the stock weight of the border
      and symbol lines on Calculator / Camera / Notes; InkApps measures the
      same on screen), outer corner radius 19.25, flush to the canvas edge
      (even-odd fill, no background fill).
    - Symbol: scan brackets + scan line, round caps and joins, stroke 2.7
      (the artwork's weight, a deliberate exception to the stock 2.5), on a
      37.8-unit centerline square with corner radius 4.5; outer extent
      20.25..60.75 (54px on the launcher).
    - Pixel-snapped for the Kompakt launcher, which draws icons at exactly
      108px (4/3 px per unit, whole pixels at multiples of 0.75 units):
      every straight line's outer edge sits on a whole pixel, so it renders
      like the border, 3 solid px + 1 gray edge px, rather than straddling
      pixels with gray on both sides, which reads soft on e-ink. This moves
      each line a third of a pixel at most from where the artist drew it.
      The scan line's top edge is the snapped one (39.0 = 52px).
    - res/mipmap-xxxhdpi/ic_launcher.png is not used by the app. It is a 192px
      render of this icon (a copy of icons/launcher-192.png) kept at the old
      launcher path because pages outside the repo link to its
      raw.githubusercontent.com URL. Re-export it whenever this icon changes.
    Source: icons/launcher.svg
-->
